1
00:00:03,023 --> 00:00:06,033
天啊 那双手冰凉刺骨啊
Oh,my goodness,those hands are cold.

2
00:00:06,363 --> 00:00:09,564
至少让我做个饱死鬼啊
At least, buy me dinner first.

3
00:00:10,214 --> 00:00:13,184
告诉我的妻子孩子我爱它们
Tell my wife and kids I love them.

4
00:00:13,184 --> 00:00:14,624
天啊
Oh, my god.

5
00:00:14,624 --> 00:00:16,644
你瞬间把故事变黑暗了 妈
That's kind of dark, mom.

6
00:00:16,644 --> 00:00:17,624
什么啊
What

7
00:00:17,784 --> 00:00:19,555
等等 我最爱的医院食物是什么
Wait, what's my favourite hospital food?

8
00:00:20,165 --> 00:00:21,585
哈露[哈啰+吉露果冻]
Jell-o!

9
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:23,445
好啊 哥们儿
Hi, buddy.

10
00:00:23,465 --> 00:00:24,525
不 今天可以的
No, today is so good.

11
00:00:24,535 --> 00:00:25,785
什么可以 哪个哥们儿
Good for what? Who's buddy?

12
00:00:25,785 --> 00:00:27,605
好啊 直接来屋子里见面吧
Yeah, just head over on to the house.

13
00:00:27,605 --> 00:00:29,016
谁家屋子 哥们儿又是谁
Whose house?who's buddy?

14
00:00:29,016 --> 00:00:30,436
行 一会儿见
OK, see you in a couple.

15
00:00:30,436 --> 00:00:31,906
一对什么 哥们儿是谁
Couple of what? Who's buddy?

16
00:00:31,906 --> 00:00:32,666
肯尼斯
Kenneth.

17
00:00:32,666 --> 00:00:34,606
-肯尼斯 -肯尼斯
- Kenneth? - Kenneth!

18
00:00:34,956 --> 00:00:37,226
如果我有儿子 我想他能和肯尼斯·普洛弗一样
If I had a son, I'd want him to be like Kenneth Ploufe.

19
00:00:37,226 --> 00:00:37,996
你确实是有儿子的
You do have a son.

20
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:38,916
我们刚搬来这里时
When we first moved in here,

21
00:00:38,916 --> 00:00:40,587
他还是个可爱的小孩 住在我们隔壁
He was the sweet kid who lived next door.

22
00:00:40,587 --> 00:00:41,637
是住在我们隔壁的古怪小孩吧
Mm, the weird kid who lived next door,

23
00:00:41,647 --> 00:00:43,627
但菲尔对他很亲
But Phil always had a soft spot for him

24
00:00:43,627 --> 00:00:45,187
因为肯尼斯有点敬仰他
Because Kenneth sort of looked up to him.

25
00:00:45,197 --> 00:00:46,727
我都不想说他视我如英雄
I wouldn't say hero.

26
00:00:46,777 --> 00:00:47,767
但你还是说了
And yet you did.

27
00:00:47,767 --> 00:00:49,157
因为你不打算说啊
Well, you weren't going to.

28
00:00:50,128 --> 00:00:52,178
克莱尔对肯尼斯有些成见
Claire's always had some issues with Kenneth.

29
00:00:52,178 --> 00:00:54,638
他老是色迷迷地盯着我看
He would stare at me a little too long.

30
00:00:54,828 --> 00:00:56,258
那能怪他吗
Can you blame him?

31
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,898
因为你当年穿得太性感了
You used to dress sexy back then.

32
00:01:07,469 --> 00:01:09,069
一晃十年过去了 难以置信啊
Ten years. Can you believe it?

33
00:01:10,399 --> 00:01:12,180
我觉得刚刚的拥抱过于仓促
I feel like we ended that last hug too soon.

34
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,340
再来一个吧
I-- come on again!

35
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:16,480
哦 抱的多了点吧
Oh, wow, that's a lot of hugging.

36
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,610
她说得对 为什么要拥抱 明明可以直接...
Oh! She's right. Why hug when you can...

37
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:20,970
-爷们握手 -爷们握手
- Man-shake. - Man-shake.

38
00:01:25,601 --> 00:01:27,011
我去弄咖啡
I'm gonna get the coffee.

39
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:29,481
爷们握手
"Man-shake."

40
00:01:29,841 --> 00:01:30,991
没搞错吧
Are we sure?

41
00:01:33,492 --> 00:01:34,972
拉起"门帘"
Roll up the curtain.

42
00:01:50,223 --> 00:01:51,093
我都不知道哪样才更糟
I don't know what's worse--

43
00:01:51,093 --> 00:01:54,103
是他每年感恩节都会参加吃派比赛
That he competes every thanksgiving in a pie-eating contest,

44
00:01:54,103 --> 00:01:55,904
还是他已经9次屈居第二了
or that he's 9-time runner-up.

45
00:01:56,364 --> 00:01:58,364
没有比赛 就不是感恩节了
It wouldn't be thanksgiving without the contest.

46
00:01:58,364 --> 00:01:59,544
当然也是啊
Yes, it would.

47
00:02:00,144 --> 00:02:01,934
我好想说说我的射南瓜故事
I think I have to tell my pumpkin chunkin story.

48
00:02:01,934 --> 00:02:03,274
不不不 你不需要说的
Oh, no, no, you don't have to.

49
00:02:03,274 --> 00:02:04,894
不 我觉得我必须说
No, I kind of think I have to.

50
00:02:05,635 --> 00:02:06,615
有次 小卡和他的朋友们
Once, Cam and his friends

51
00:02:06,615 --> 00:02:09,345
试着将南瓜从足球场的一端射到另一端的
tried to slingshot a pumpkin across a football field.

52
00:02:10,575 --> 00:02:11,205
3秒钟
Three seconds.

53
00:02:11,205 --> 00:02:12,625
3秒种就可以讲完那个故事
That's all he needs to tell that story.

54
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:14,995
山间大雾弥漫
So the fog was rolling in over the mountains

55
00:02:14,995 --> 00:02:16,636
像是覆盖了一条不祥的毯子
Like an ominous blanket

56
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:18,926
正当我们准备好弹弓时
As we readied the giant slingshot.

57
00:02:18,926 --> 00:02:20,436
牧师的女儿 洛娜
You know, Lorna, the pastor's daughter,

58
00:02:20,436 --> 00:02:23,606
她很紧张 因为当时已经是宵禁后了
She was nervous because like I said, it was after curfew.

59
00:02:23,616 --> 00:02:24,996
她是个"冒牌天使"
She was a goody two-shoe.

60
00:02:24,996 --> 00:02:27,827
我遇见的牧师女儿里就她是那样的
Only pastor's daughter I ever met that was.

61
00:02:31,417 --> 00:02:32,907
最终我们将南瓜装上弓
So we finally launch the pumpkin,

62
00:02:32,907 --> 00:02:36,257
南瓜在空中飞过 穿越一个个门柱
And it sails through the air, goalpost to goalpost...

63
00:02:36,257 --> 00:02:38,998
穿过球门区 直击停车场
Past the end zone, into the parking lot,

64
00:02:38,998 --> 00:02:41,558
又穿过洛娜父亲车子的露顶
Through the open roof of Lorna's dad's car.

65
00:02:41,568 --> 00:02:43,678
我转身对科迪说
I turn to Cody and I say,

66
00:02:43,708 --> 00:02:46,608
射到那里的几率有多大
"Now what are the chances of that landing there?"

67
00:02:46,608 --> 00:02:48,039
他说 哪里
He says, "Where?"

68
00:02:48,039 --> 00:02:49,589
然后我说
And I say...

69
00:02:50,099 --> 00:02:52,479
牧师的汽车天窗
"The sunroof of a preacher man."

70
00:02:54,569 --> 00:02:55,909
哇哇
Wah-wah

71
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:03,460
好了 进来吧
Okay, come on in!

72
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:05,820
瞧啊
Voila!

73
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,390
好吧 眼前是什么玩意儿呢
Ah! Okay, what are we looking at?

74
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:11,411
真是太棒了 你真有才
It is wonderful. You're so talented.

75
00:03:11,411 --> 00:03:13,281
我真不敢相信你做了这个
I can't believe that you did this.

76
00:03:13,281 --> 00:03:15,781
是吧 我自己欣赏的时候 也口水直流
Yeah, my juices were really flowing on this one.

77
00:03:17,581 --> 00:03:19,491
我们可以在派对结束后观看
Hey, maybe we can watch it later at the party.

78
00:03:19,501 --> 00:03:20,892
或者看橄榄球赛吧
Well, yeah, that or football.

79
00:03:22,412 --> 00:03:24,702
小宝贝 我真为你骄傲
Mi amor, I'm so proud of you.

80
00:03:24,702 --> 00:03:27,702
世界上还有什么是你做不到的吗
Is there nothing in the world that you can't do?

81
00:03:27,702 --> 00:03:29,232
餐桌中央摆饰 就算第一件了
Centerpieces, for starters.

82
00:03:29,532 --> 00:03:31,273
你为什么说他做的一切都很棒
Why do you say everything of his is great,

83
00:03:31,273 --> 00:03:32,093
即便实际上很烂
Even if it isn't?

84
00:03:32,093 --> 00:03:34,273
因为我在给他树立信心
Because I'm building him up.

85
00:03:34,373 --> 00:03:35,513
那是父母的任务之一
That's what parents do.

86
00:03:35,513 --> 00:03:36,623
要我说的话 你做的太过了
Too much, if you ask me.

87
00:03:36,623 --> 00:03:38,623
现在的孩子会过马路 就能得到朵小红花
Kids cross the street nowadays, they get a ribbon.

88
00:03:38,663 --> 00:03:40,033
曼尼已经自信心爆棚了
Manny's got plenty of confidence.

89
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:42,824
他需要的是对现实的偶尔清醒认识
He just needs a little reality check every now and then.

90
00:03:42,834 --> 00:03:44,994
这玩意儿简直丑伤了
And this thing is a horn of ugly.

91
00:03:44,994 --> 00:03:46,004
嘘
Shh!

92
00:03:46,004 --> 00:03:48,664
我妈妈以前总是批评我所做的一切
My mother used to criticize everything I did.

93
00:03:48,794 --> 00:03:50,324
瞧瞧现在的我
And look at me now.

94
00:03:50,324 --> 00:03:52,374
就是个缺乏安全感的可怜虫
I am a jumble of insecurities.

95
00:03:52,645 --> 00:03:53,665
我不懂
I'm not getting that.

96
00:03:53,665 --> 00:03:55,855
绝对不许打击曼尼
Do not say a word to Manny.

97
00:03:55,855 --> 00:03:57,615
好吧 不过相信我
Fine. But trust me,

98
00:03:57,785 --> 00:04:00,425
如果你告诉他实情 他以后会感激你的
If you told him the truth, he'd thank you later.

99
00:04:01,055 --> 00:04:03,566
像克莱尔和米奇一样吗 他们感谢过你吗
Mm. Like Claire and Mitch? Did they thank you?

100
00:04:03,566 --> 00:04:04,666
暂时还没
Not yet.

101
00:04:05,186 --> 00:04:06,396
但很快就会的
But it's coming.

102
00:04:10,396 --> 00:04:12,476
这里充满了我的回忆啊
Ah! So many memories in this place. Yeah.

103
00:04:12,636 --> 00:04:14,187
你们依然 每次吃麦片的时候都那个吗
Do you guys still have, like, every cereal?

104
00:04:14,187 --> 00:04:15,047
必须的
We have a lot.

105
00:04:15,047 --> 00:04:17,057
当然当然 那是肯定的啦
Yeah! Of course you do. Of course you do.

106
00:04:17,057 --> 00:04:18,947
你们有世上最了不起的老爸
You only have the greatest dad in the world.

107
00:04:19,447 --> 00:04:20,227
你近些年在忙些什么啊
So what have you been up to?

108
00:04:20,227 --> 00:04:21,867
你上大学后 我就没见过你了
I haven't seen you since you went off to college.

109
00:04:21,867 --> 00:04:24,017
事实上 我是被大学上了
Oh, you know, actually, that didn't work out so well.

110
00:04:24,017 --> 00:04:25,478
我四处混了一段时间
I bounced around for a while.

111
00:04:25,478 --> 00:04:27,638
最后在新墨西哥州洗起了盘子
Ended up washing dishes in New Mexico.

112
00:04:27,948 --> 00:04:30,308
看来没有大学文凭
So without the benefit of a college degree,

113
00:04:30,308 --> 00:04:32,408
可以选择的职业很有限啊
I guess your options were kind of limited, huh?

114
00:04:32,738 --> 00:04:34,078
别谈学习 今天过节呢
Ease up. It's a holiday.

115
00:04:34,078 --> 00:04:36,319
是啊 是很艰难 不 不 谢谢
Yeah, it was--it was tough. Oh, no. no, thank you.

116
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:38,139
-谢谢你 甜心 你真好 -好吧
- Thank you, though, sweetie. You're so sweet. - Oh. Okay.

117
00:04:38,139 --> 00:04:39,069
一开始挺艰难的
It was tough for a while...

118
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:41,519
后来我跟我室友自己创业了
But then a roommate and I started our own business.

119
00:04:41,519 --> 00:04:44,299
也是餐饮业或清洁行业的吗
Oh, was that also in the dish or cleaning industry?

120
00:04:44,299 --> 00:04:45,459
不不
No. No, no, no.

121
00:04:45,459 --> 00:04:47,080
其实是个小投资公司
It was actually a small investment company.

122
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,630
最初规模很小
Well, small at first.

123
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:50,560
当了一阵科技的弄潮儿
You know, we rode the tech wave for a while,

124
00:04:50,710 --> 00:04:52,310
然后扩张到电子游戏
then expanded into video games,

125
00:04:52,310 --> 00:04:54,440
游乐场 运动场什么的
amusement parks, sports arenas.

126
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,420
什么牛逼就投资什么
Anything that seemed awesome, really.

127
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:58,091
我此次回乡是来买小飞艇的
I'm actually in town to buy a blimp.

128
00:04:58,091 --> 00:05:00,261
苍天大地啊
Holy crow.

129
00:05:00,871 --> 00:05:02,851
所以如果当初你上了大学
So if you--if you'd gone to college,

130
00:05:02,861 --> 00:05:05,181
可能要4年之后才会做那些事
you would have done all that just four years later,

131
00:05:05,181 --> 00:05:06,591
或者根本不会
or--or never.

132
00:05:06,671 --> 00:05:08,382
得有人去接艾丽克斯了
Alex really needs to be picked up,

133
00:05:08,382 --> 00:05:09,932
甜心 你去接下她吧
Sweetie. Why don't you go get her?

134
00:05:09,932 --> 00:05:11,732
我还想听听他的创业史呢
I wanna hear more of what he has to say about

135
00:05:11,732 --> 00:05:12,372
快走吧
We're leaving.

136
00:05:12,692 --> 00:05:15,272
肯尼斯 我太为你骄傲了
Kenneth, I am so proud of you.

137
00:05:15,602 --> 00:05:16,772
你真的很成功
You really made it.

138
00:05:17,012 --> 00:05:19,053
确实 我运气好
Well, I did get one pretty lucky break.

139
00:05:20,183 --> 00:05:22,903
早些年 我认识了个贵人
Early on, I met a very special guy

140
00:05:22,993 --> 00:05:26,363
他让我意识到我的所思所言都是有价值的
who taught me that what I thought and said had value.

141
00:05:26,673 --> 00:05:27,573
你是说...
Oh, you mean like--

142
00:05:27,573 --> 00:05:29,684
卢克 听他说
Shh. Luke. Let the man talk.

143
00:05:29,684 --> 00:05:31,764
他鼓励我干什么都得找到乐趣
He encouraged me to always find the fun

144
00:05:32,014 --> 00:05:33,674
并且永远跟着这里走
and follow this thing.

145
00:05:33,674 --> 00:05:35,284
-你的肺吗 -不 我的心
- Your lung? - No, my heart.

146
00:05:35,574 --> 00:05:37,384
直到今天 每做一个决定前
To this day, at every crossroad,

147
00:05:37,384 --> 00:05:39,274
我都会问自己
I ask myself one question--

148
00:05:40,015 --> 00:05:41,495
菲尔·邓菲会怎么做
What would Phil Dunphy do?

149
00:05:41,495 --> 00:05:43,885
至理名言啊
Record scratch!

150
00:05:43,995 --> 00:05:45,345
来电话了
Oh, that's me buzzin'.

151
00:05:45,755 --> 00:05:47,245
是帕丽斯打来的
Oh, it's Paris.

152
00:05:47,705 --> 00:05:49,285
她是我在东京的助理
She's my assistant in Tokyo.

153
00:05:49,865 --> 00:05:53,536
他们没我连个4D游戏图都展示不了
You'd think they'd know how to demo 4-d gaming graphics without my help

154
00:05:53,536 --> 00:05:55,076
完全搞不定 嘿 卢克
They don't. Hey, luke,

155
00:05:55,076 --> 00:05:57,066
马友友拉什么乐器来着
what instrument does Yo-Yo Ma play?

156
00:05:57,316 --> 00:05:58,416
"琴"讲
Um... cello?

157
00:05:59,516 --> 00:06:00,696
他就是翻版的我
He's me...

158
00:06:01,187 --> 00:06:02,797
但却是豪华升级版的
And he's spectacular.

159
00:06:04,557 --> 00:06:05,637
天啊
Oh, my god.

160
00:06:05,767 --> 00:06:09,117
肯尼斯·普洛弗与人共有在巴哈马的度假村
Kenneth Ploufe is part owner of a resort in the Bahamas,

161
00:06:09,177 --> 00:06:10,797
某条游轮巡航线
some cruise line,

162
00:06:11,187 --> 00:06:13,568
以及"蕾丝娇女" 那家内衣公司
And Lacy Fair, that lingerie company.

163
00:06:13,568 --> 00:06:15,948
恶心 我正穿着他家的胸罩呢
Oh! Ew! I'm wearing one of his bras!

164
00:06:15,948 --> 00:06:17,618
看这个 模特坐他腿上合照呢
Look, he's got a model in his lap.

165
00:06:17,618 --> 00:06:19,198
-不是吧 -看看她
- No way. - Look at her.

166
00:06:25,169 --> 00:06:26,679
都是你的错
This is your fault!

167
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:35,240
你真想一天都躲在家不出去吗
Are you seriously gonna stay in here all day?

168
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,510
我无法面对妈妈
I can't face mom.

169
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:38,370
我一看见她 就会忍不住坦白从宽的
If I see her, I'm gonna have to confess.

170
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:41,170
淡定 不过就是有点小凹
Take a breather. It's just a dent.

171
00:06:41,170 --> 00:06:44,091
沉默不是撒谎 好吗
And saying nothing is not lying, okay?

172
00:06:44,101 --> 00:06:46,551
只是让真相自己大白而已
It's just letting the truth speak for itself.

173
00:06:46,551 --> 00:06:48,871
现在不是模糊道义责任的时候
This is not the time for moral equivocation.

174
00:06:48,871 --> 00:06:50,201
我不知道那是什么意思
Okay, I don't know what that means,

175
00:06:50,211 --> 00:06:52,081
也不想知道
and also, don't tell me.

176
00:06:52,081 --> 00:06:53,761
你才是那个以后不能碰车的人
You're the one who's gonna lose her driving privileges.

177
00:06:53,761 --> 00:06:55,312
你怎么能这么冷静
I don't know why you're so calm.

178
00:06:55,312 --> 00:06:57,342
我们只要暂时瞒住妈妈
All we have to do is keep it from mom

179
00:06:57,352 --> 00:06:58,852
一直瞒到她去商店就行了
until she goes to the store.

180
00:06:58,852 --> 00:07:02,072
然后 她发现了的话 也会觉得是在商店撞的
Then, when she sees it, she'll assume that it happened there,

181
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:05,192
本来也就确实是 所以根本不算撒谎
which it did, so it's not really lying.

182
00:07:05,362 --> 00:07:06,673
听听 你说谎都不打草稿
Listen to you.

183
00:07:07,113 --> 00:07:08,683
你是想成为职业罪犯吗
Are you gonna be a career criminal?

184
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:09,943
你跟妈妈简直一模一样
Ugh. You sound like mom.

185
00:07:09,943 --> 00:07:12,363
我高中毕业后可怎么办啊
I don't know what I'm gonna do after high school.

186
00:07:13,663 --> 00:07:15,453
我那声"哇哇"是表达对你的支持
It was a supportive "Wah-wah."

187
00:07:15,453 --> 00:07:16,414
不让你冷场
I was trying to save the moment.

188
00:07:16,424 --> 00:07:18,684
"哇哇"那种声音怎么可能表示支持
There's no such thing as a supportive "Wah-wah."

189
00:07:18,694 --> 00:07:20,964
那个声调就是讽刺和侮辱的代名词
A "Wah-wah" By its very nature is vicious and undercutting.

190
00:07:20,964 --> 00:07:22,954
我只是为了替你的故事打圆场
Well, I was just trying to salvage that story, okay?

191
00:07:22,954 --> 00:07:24,134
我叫你别说
I told you not to tell it,

192
00:07:24,134 --> 00:07:25,644
你还是说了 结果场子砸了
You told it, and it died.

193
00:07:25,644 --> 00:07:27,275
没砸 只是他们没反应过来
It did not die. It's a thinker.

194
00:07:27,275 --> 00:07:28,395
小卡 他们在想的唯一一件事就是
Cam, the only thing people were thinking was,

195
00:07:28,395 --> 00:07:30,185
"谢天谢地他总算说完了"
"Thank god this story's over."

196
00:07:30,505 --> 00:07:31,405
好吧 我明白了
Okay. I get it.

197
00:07:31,405 --> 00:07:33,625
我的故事让你觉得丢人有多久了
So how long have I been embarrassing you with my stories?

198
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:35,315
不不 你没有丢我的人
No, no, no, no. You don't embarrass me.

199
00:07:35,325 --> 00:07:37,095
我爱你的故事
I love your stories, okay?

200
00:07:37,095 --> 00:07:38,656
水塘里的拖拉机
The tractor in the swimming hole?

201
00:07:38,736 --> 00:07:40,696
把贝蒂婶的假发戴到猪崽头上
Aunt Betty's wiglet on the piglet?

202
00:07:41,016 --> 00:07:42,766
卡尔叔说她分不清那些小猪崽
Uncle Carl said she couldn't tell 'em apart.

203
00:07:42,876 --> 00:07:45,726
是吧 好好笑啊 多么五彩斑斓的童年趣事啊
See? Those are funny. You have so many great ones.

204
00:07:45,726 --> 00:07:46,636
农场生活就是如此
Well, that's farm life.

205
00:07:46,636 --> 00:07:48,657
无论下雨或天晴 精彩故事永不停
Rain or shine, there's always a bumper crop of stories.

206
00:07:48,657 --> 00:07:49,667
是啊 我的意思是
Yeah, I'm just saying maybe

207
00:07:49,667 --> 00:07:51,757
你该让那个射南瓜的故事退居二线了
you take punkin chunkin out of the rotation.

208
00:07:52,037 --> 00:07:53,317
你说得也有理 或许我可以...
I guess you're right. Maybe I could just--

209
00:07:53,317 --> 00:07:54,557
是啊 就讲那些真实发生过的事
Yeah, stick to the ones that really happened,

210
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,057
人们都喜欢真实的故事
because people love those.

211
00:07:56,677 --> 00:07:57,847
不好意思 你说什么
Excuse me. What?

212
00:07:58,147 --> 00:08:00,758
我的意思是 真事才更有笑点
I'm--I'm just saying people laugh more at stories that are true.

213
00:08:00,758 --> 00:08:02,408
射南瓜是真人真事
Punkin chunkin is a true story.

214
00:08:02,508 --> 00:08:03,708
有点真实?
True-ish?

215
00:08:03,708 --> 00:08:05,708
不 完全真实
No. True.

216
00:08:05,838 --> 00:08:06,908
是吗
Really?

217
00:08:07,378 --> 00:08:08,818
橄榄球场那么大
The length of a football field,

218
00:08:08,818 --> 00:08:13,219
11月底的密苏里 车的天窗还是开着的?
Through the sunroof of a car that was open in late november in Missouri?

219
00:08:13,219 --> 00:08:14,629
那年秋老虎很猖狂
It was unseasonably warm.

220
00:08:14,629 --> 00:08:16,549
所以山间雾气弥漫?
That explains the fog rolling over the hill.

221
00:08:16,559 --> 00:08:17,839
还有科迪是谁
And who's Cody--

222
00:08:17,959 --> 00:08:19,519
你可以熟到跟他一起射南瓜
Who you're close enough to chunk with

223
00:08:19,519 --> 00:08:21,850
但除此之外却从来没提起过他
but mysteriously only appears in this story?

224
00:08:21,850 --> 00:08:23,550
科迪在沙漠风暴行动中不幸阵亡
Cody was K.I.A. In desert storm.

225
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,690
他是个英雄
He's a hero.

226
00:08:27,810 --> 00:08:29,110
你根本没资格质疑
You know, all this from someone

227
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:31,330
因为你从来没有发射过南瓜
who's never even chunked a punkin.

228
00:08:32,631 --> 00:08:34,051
我可没丢人丢到家呢
Well, I've never lunked a tunkin, either.

229
00:08:34,051 --> 00:08:35,881
因为 那些都不是真事
You know, these aren't real things.

230
00:08:37,011 --> 00:08:38,341
这样可以吧
This'll work, right?

231
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:39,301
绝对行 老爸
Totally, dad.

232
00:08:39,301 --> 00:08:40,401
干嘛要用一张长桌呢
Why have one long table

233
00:08:40,401 --> 00:08:43,052
明明可以用4个酒馆小餐桌
when you can use four little ones bistro style?

234
00:08:43,532 --> 00:08:45,532
法国人肯定就是这么过感恩节的
I'll bet this is how the French do Thanksgiving.

235
00:08:45,872 --> 00:08:47,172
你不介意跟你米奇舅舅
You don't mind sitting with your Uncle Mitch

236
00:08:47,172 --> 00:08:48,632
还有外公一起坐吧
And, uh, grandpa, do you?

237
00:08:48,642 --> 00:08:51,202
只要不用看莉莉吧唧嘴 坐哪儿都行
Anything's better than watching Lily chew.

238
00:08:51,202 --> 00:08:52,192
随便一提
By the way,

239
00:08:52,192 --> 00:08:55,343
这就是肯尼斯所说的你老爹的另一面
this is the side of your old man that Kenneth was talking about.

240
00:08:55,343 --> 00:08:56,593
创意十足
Original.

241
00:08:57,033 --> 00:08:58,863
天马行空
Imaginative.

242
00:09:00,943 --> 00:09:02,263
无所畏惧
Fearless.

243
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:05,584
肯尼斯成为亿万富翁是因为他
So Kenneth became a gajillionaire

244
00:09:05,584 --> 00:09:07,754
常常扪心自问 如果是菲尔会怎么做吗
by asking himself, "What would Phil do?"

245
00:09:08,444 --> 00:09:10,104
是的没错
He sure did.

246
00:09:11,124 --> 00:09:13,134
真是神来之笔啊 对吧
Where did that come from? Right?

247
00:09:13,704 --> 00:09:15,585
可你是原版的菲尔
But you're you.

248
00:09:15,745 --> 00:09:17,465
我们怎么没变亿万富翁
Why aren't we gojillionaires?

249
00:09:17,475 --> 00:09:19,345
为什么你不按照菲尔的想法去做呢
Why don't you do what Phil would do?

250
00:09:20,195 --> 00:09:24,095
菲尔 干嘛不把桌子都拼起来
Phil, why didn't you just put the extra leaves in the table?

251
00:09:24,275 --> 00:09:26,566
我想试着来点好玩的 搞点创意
Trying to have some fun, be creative.

252
00:09:26,606 --> 00:09:28,246
拼成一长桌子吧 亲爱的
One long table, honey.

253
00:09:28,246 --> 00:09:29,946
耶稣最后的晚餐用的就是长桌
If it was good enough for the last supper,

254
00:09:29,946 --> 00:09:31,176
我们也该效仿
it's good enough for us.

255
00:09:35,256 --> 00:09:37,547
关于我做的餐桌摆饰 我有点犹豫了
I'm having second thoughts about this centerpiece.

256
00:09:37,547 --> 00:09:39,317
-别想了 -听他说下去
- Ay, no. - Hear him out.

257
00:09:39,327 --> 00:09:40,987
要是我们带它去菲尔和克莱尔家
I just think if we bring it to Phil and Claire's,

258
00:09:40,987 --> 00:09:42,387
就再也见不到它了是吧
we'll never see it again, right?

259
00:09:42,397 --> 00:09:43,337
是的
That's the plan.

260
00:09:43,337 --> 00:09:44,857
那真让人伤心
Well, that would be sad.

261
00:09:45,507 --> 00:09:47,328
不过这份伤感或许能激发我
Except maybe my sadness will inspire me

262
00:09:47,328 --> 00:09:49,168
创造出更棒的作品
to create something even greater.

263
00:09:49,398 --> 00:09:50,438
记得我做的那副拼贴画吗
Remember that collage I made

264
00:09:50,448 --> 00:09:52,478
是它支撑我们度过了卡特里娜飓风危机
that helped us get through Katrina?

265
00:09:52,478 --> 00:09:53,818
都是你造成的 你明白吧
You did this. You know that.

266
00:09:53,818 --> 00:09:54,598
难道
So...

267
00:09:54,598 --> 00:09:57,689
那就是江湖上闻名已久的手抓饭吗
is this the legendary rice pilaf we've been hearing about?

268
00:09:57,689 --> 00:09:58,559
你自己尝尝
Try for yourself.

269
00:09:58,849 --> 00:09:59,639
以前我每年都做这个
Used to make it every year,

270
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:02,339
但后来它开始抢走了烤火鸡的风头
but it, uh, started to upstage the turkey.

271
00:10:03,819 --> 00:10:07,249
-不好吃吗 -不至于到难吃
- Something wrong? - Not so much wrong as missing.

272
00:10:07,589 --> 00:10:09,280
只是略显平淡无味
It--it just tastes a little flat.

273
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,400
是吗
That a fact?

274
00:10:10,570 --> 00:10:12,130
我只是觉得可以加些辛香料
I just think with the earthiness of the rice,

275
00:10:12,130 --> 00:10:14,390
来盖过米饭的土腥味
you might want something zesty to set it off.

276
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,200
估计加点孜然能管用
I think this might be a job for cumin.

277
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,110
既然我们在相互交流
You know, since we're sharing

278
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,260
-批评指正 -停停停
- helpful criticisms-- - no, no, no, no.

279
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:21,091
谁都别再说了 曼尼 去换衣服
nobody's sharing anything. Manny, go change for the party.

280
00:10:21,091 --> 00:10:23,151
可是我愿意听取善意的批评
No, no, no, but I appreciate helpful criticisms.

281
00:10:23,151 --> 00:10:26,291
我觉得知道真相十分重要
It, uh, it's important for me that I hear the truth.

282
00:10:26,291 --> 00:10:27,661
能令我更坚强
Makes me stronger,

283
00:10:27,791 --> 00:10:29,782
而不只是个离不开妈的孩子
less of a mama's boy.

284
00:10:29,872 --> 00:10:31,102
没错 妈 他承受得了
Yeah, mom, he can take it.

285
00:10:31,102 --> 00:10:32,112
他嘴巴上这么说
That's what he says,

286
00:10:32,122 --> 00:10:35,852
可你不知道他内心实际的感受
but you don't really know what he feels underneath.

287
00:10:35,932 --> 00:10:37,812
有些人太过敏感
Some people are so sensitive,

288
00:10:37,812 --> 00:10:39,812
一句批评
that they hear one criticism,

289
00:10:39,822 --> 00:10:43,493
就能毁掉他们的才华
and it kills the spark that made them special.

290
00:10:43,613 --> 00:10:45,183
我明白是怎么回事了
I think I know what's going on here.

291
00:10:45,183 --> 00:10:45,993
太好了
Good.

292
00:10:45,993 --> 00:10:47,913
是有关你和你妈之间的纠葛 对吧
This is about you and your mom, isn't it?

293
00:10:48,163 --> 00:10:48,873
对 没错
Yes, it is.

294
00:10:48,873 --> 00:10:49,563
不 不是的
No, it isn't.

295
00:10:49,563 --> 00:10:51,104
就是那样
Yes, it is!

296
00:10:51,294 --> 00:10:52,804
曼尼 别再让我心烦了
Manny, don't upset me anymore.

297
00:10:52,814 --> 00:10:54,414
去 换衣服去吧
Go. Go change.

298
00:10:55,284 --> 00:10:56,394
我该穿什么啊
What--what should I wear?

299
00:10:56,394 --> 00:10:58,774
你穿啥都好看
Ay, you look good in everything!

300
00:11:03,945 --> 00:11:04,985
你去哪儿啊 妈妈
Where you going, mom?

301
00:11:05,025 --> 00:11:06,985
得去趟商店
Mm, I gotta run to the store.

302
00:11:07,015 --> 00:11:08,795
有人把棉花糖都吃完了
Someone ate all the marshmallows.

303
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,675
能跟你商量点事吗
Hey, can I tell you something?

304
00:11:11,115 --> 00:11:13,856
我在考虑寒假以后
I was thinking that maybe after new year's break,

305
00:11:13,886 --> 00:11:15,326
我们可以去其他的大学看一看
we could visit a couple more colleges.

306
00:11:15,326 --> 00:11:18,196
-你说真的吗 -我之前对你太凶了
- Seriously? - I was so hard on you before.

307
00:11:18,226 --> 00:11:19,926
抱歉 我明白我做不到肯尼斯那样
I'm sorry. I know I'm no Kenneth.

308
00:11:19,966 --> 00:11:21,996
我得尽量取得别人的帮助
I'm gonna need all the help that I can get.

309
00:11:22,036 --> 00:11:25,297
亲爱的 我为你骄傲
Honey, I am so proud of you. Oh.

310
00:11:25,337 --> 00:11:27,367
谢了
Oh, thank you.

311
00:11:28,147 --> 00:11:29,307
什么呀
What's this?

312
00:11:29,337 --> 00:11:30,737
-好吧 -怎么了
- Oh, okay. - What are you doing?

313
00:11:30,777 --> 00:11:32,077
米奇舅舅已经在买棉花糖了
Oh, uncle Mitch is picking up the marshmallows.

314
00:11:32,107 --> 00:11:33,277
话说回来 去欧洲背包游
Then again, backpacking through Europe

315
00:11:33,307 --> 00:11:34,878
也有其独特的教育意义吧
could be educational in its own way.

316
00:11:34,918 --> 00:11:36,578
别 别 别
No! No, no! No, no, no!

317
00:11:36,618 --> 00:11:38,498
你知道在欧洲什么算违法吗
Do you know what's illegal in Europe?

318
00:11:38,498 --> 00:11:39,438
啥都不违法
Nothing!

319
00:11:39,438 --> 00:11:41,058
你上大学上定了
You are going to college!

320
00:11:41,058 --> 00:11:42,418
好吧 随你
Okay, fine.

321
00:11:42,458 --> 00:11:43,788
当然是听我的
Darn right it's fine.

322
00:11:45,759 --> 00:11:47,059
手到擒来
Piece of cake.

323
00:11:48,969 --> 00:11:50,499
我头发都要吓掉了
My hair's coming out!

324
00:11:52,409 --> 00:11:54,989
亲爱的 我以为你会布置得简单点
Wow, honey. I-I think you could make these simpler.

325
00:11:54,989 --> 00:11:57,580
将一边平铺开就可以了
Just, you know, sort of do 'em flat and on the side.

326
00:11:57,610 --> 00:11:59,830
就像你希望我成为的那样
Hmm. Yeah. Seems like that's how you like me.

327
00:11:59,830 --> 00:12:01,410
平平淡淡 甘居下游
Flat and on the side.

328
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,150
有时我也需要膨胀一下 摆摆架子
You know what? Sometimes I need to be puffed up and frilly.

329
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:05,130
要是以后人家问起
All right, is this one of

330
00:12:05,130 --> 00:12:06,221
咱俩婚姻破裂前的征兆之一
those moments I'm gonna have to remember later

331
00:12:06,221 --> 00:12:08,391
我是否就该想到此时此刻呀
when they ask me if there were any signs?

332
00:12:08,391 --> 00:12:09,821
这就是菲尔会做的事
This is what Phil would do--

333
00:12:09,861 --> 00:12:11,521
把餐巾折得有模有样
Make fantastic napkin origami

334
00:12:11,561 --> 00:12:13,611
令客人们又惊又喜
that startles and delights his guests.

335
00:12:13,611 --> 00:12:14,671
我知道 可亲爱的
I know, but, sweetie,

336
00:12:14,671 --> 00:12:17,142
它们看起来有点...
they're just looking a little...

337
00:12:17,182 --> 00:12:20,052
克莱尔 你总是这样 你总打击我
Claire, you always do this. You squelch me.

338
00:12:20,082 --> 00:12:22,422
每当我要展翅高飞时 你就打击我
You squelch me right when I'm about to soar.

339
00:12:22,452 --> 00:12:24,022
亲爱的 你只是折个餐巾而已
Honey, you're folding napkins.

340
00:12:24,052 --> 00:12:25,882
你在屈折我的梦想
You're folding my dreams!

341
00:12:26,332 --> 00:12:27,943
你知道肯尼斯说了什么吗
You know what Kenneth told me?

342
00:12:27,943 --> 00:12:29,563
他事业成功的奥秘
The secret to his success--

343
00:12:29,563 --> 00:12:32,413
是因为他试着模仿我
his whole career, he's tried to emulate me.

344
00:12:32,443 --> 00:12:33,413
唯一不同的是
The only difference is,

345
00:12:33,413 --> 00:12:36,613
没有人不停地要他别干这个 别干那个
he hasn't had someone constantly telling him what not to do.

346
00:12:36,653 --> 00:12:40,194
你意思是说我们家买不起小飞艇的唯一原因
So the only reason we don't have a-a blimp tethered to our mailbox

347
00:12:40,194 --> 00:12:43,194
是因为我总是打击你的"奇思妙想"
is because I'm always shooting down your great ideas?

348
00:12:43,224 --> 00:12:44,394
没错
Yeah.

349
00:12:44,424 --> 00:12:46,324
咱们回顾一下"打击史" 菲尔
Let's review the squelch pile, Phil.

350
00:12:46,364 --> 00:12:48,794
比如 米布丁的特许经销权
Let's see-- the rice pudding franchise.

351
00:12:48,824 --> 00:12:50,165
无齿之徒 也可享受
Works for all chewing abilities.

352
00:12:50,195 --> 00:12:51,565
成人三轮车
Adult tricycles.

353
00:12:51,595 --> 00:12:52,635
有种你就摔摔看
Just try to fall off.

354
00:12:52,665 --> 00:12:53,805
阿司匹林喷射枪
The Aspirin gun.

355
00:12:53,835 --> 00:12:55,975
有人就是吞药困难嘛
Some people have a hard time swallowing!

356
00:12:56,395 --> 00:12:57,805
你还忘说了一个
And you left one out. Hmm.

357
00:12:57,835 --> 00:13:00,656
亲爱的克莱尔 那才是挠破头皮才能想到的
And that, my dear claire, is a real head-scratcher--

358
00:13:00,656 --> 00:13:01,706
"不求人"
"Tm."

359
00:13:03,416 --> 00:13:04,646
开演
Action.

360
00:13:07,076 --> 00:13:07,946
朋友好啊
Hey, friend.

361
00:13:08,716 --> 00:13:10,907
看上去你今天上班累惨了吧
You look like you had a rough day at the office.

362
00:13:11,057 --> 00:13:14,387
在"机器人暗杀工厂"的工作压力真是...
The stress from my job at the robot assassin factory...

363
00:13:14,817 --> 00:13:16,697
生命中不能承受之重
Is too much to take.

364
00:13:16,897 --> 00:13:19,227
给我来一枪阿司匹林吧 亲
Aw, shoot me an aspirin, pal.

365
00:13:19,367 --> 00:13:20,827
日后再议
Maybe someday.

366
00:13:20,867 --> 00:13:23,658
不过先来试试这个合不合适
But until then, try this on for size.

367
00:13:24,308 --> 00:13:27,398
即将拥有32项专利的脑神经导体按摩仪
The real head-scratcher features 32 patent-pending "Nogginizers"

368
00:13:27,398 --> 00:13:28,978
轻柔按摩您的头部
That gently massage your scalp

369
00:13:28,978 --> 00:13:31,448
在安宁的声音中给您以享受
In a soothing purr of motorized delight.

370
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:35,079
哇塞 真舒服
Ahh. It feels great,

371
00:13:35,119 --> 00:13:37,379
外形也很帅气哦
And it looks good, too.

372
00:13:37,379 --> 00:13:39,019
真是居家旅行必备良器
It's a real lifesaver.

373
00:13:39,019 --> 00:13:40,919
您是说真正的头部按摩仪吧
You mean a real head-scratcher?

374
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:45,680
"不求人"
"Tm."

375
00:13:46,690 --> 00:13:48,360
我爱你 菲尔
I love you, Phil,

376
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,370
-但是呢 -别说了
- But you-- - Stop.

377
00:13:49,780 --> 00:13:51,250
我就爱听你说爱我
I love your "I love you."

378
00:13:51,430 --> 00:13:53,150
但我就怕温柔背后的一刀
I'm getting awful tired of your "But."

379
00:13:53,801 --> 00:13:54,831
我经历过的
I heard it.

380
00:14:11,512 --> 00:14:12,952
欢迎欢迎 热烈欢迎
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

381
00:14:12,952 --> 00:14:14,542
欢度火鸡节哦
Happy turkey day!

382
00:14:14,542 --> 00:14:15,733
哇 你们买了辆新车啊
Hey, is that a new car?

383
00:14:15,733 --> 00:14:17,213
没错 是不是特棒
Yep! It's the best, isn't it?

384
00:14:17,213 --> 00:14:18,853
我的目光简直被钉在上面了
I can't take my eyes off it.

385
00:14:19,013 --> 00:14:20,383
您也别往别处看了
You shouldn't, either.

386
00:14:20,983 --> 00:14:22,153
你还好吧 闺女
Are you okay, mami?

387
00:14:22,153 --> 00:14:23,633
我 我
I'm... I'm...

388
00:14:23,633 --> 00:14:27,084
大家好啊 派对开始了 快进去吧
Hey, guys! Now the party's started. Come on!

389
00:14:27,084 --> 00:14:28,214
-最近好吗 -很好
- How are you? - Good.

390
00:14:28,254 --> 00:14:29,434
恶心死姐了
You disgust me.

391
00:14:29,434 --> 00:14:30,454
饿坏了吧
Are you hungry?

392
00:14:30,894 --> 00:14:32,554
还好没散架
Oh, good. It's still in one piece.

393
00:14:32,594 --> 00:14:34,444
你都快把我建的洞穴弄塌方了
You hit those potholes pretty hard.

394
00:14:34,444 --> 00:14:35,384
你难道没看见吗
It's like you didn't see 'em.

395
00:14:35,384 --> 00:14:36,605
不 我看见了
No, I saw 'em.

396
00:14:37,135 --> 00:14:38,595
我能跟你说句实话吗 杰
Can I be honest with you, Jay?

397
00:14:38,595 --> 00:14:39,455
我觉得
I'm getting the sense

398
00:14:39,455 --> 00:14:41,395
你好像不那么喜欢我做的"阿雷古丽娜"
that you're not the biggest fan of "Allegria"?

399
00:14:41,425 --> 00:14:43,165
你还给它起了个名字 真棒
You got a name for it now? Great.

400
00:14:43,195 --> 00:14:44,415
好吧 要我说实话
All right. Cards on the table?

401
00:14:44,415 --> 00:14:46,405
你可以做得更好的
This is not your best work.

402
00:14:46,405 --> 00:14:48,146
听着 别会错意
Now look, don't get me wrong.

403
00:14:48,206 --> 00:14:49,476
你挺有才的
You're a talented kid.

404
00:14:49,506 --> 00:14:50,746
终有一天你会展翅翱翔
You're gonna be a big success in the world.

405
00:14:50,746 --> 00:14:53,336
但这个 纯粹是瞎胡闹嘛
But this... this is a swing and a miss.

406
00:14:53,336 --> 00:14:55,956
-不过妈说 -你妈说很好 我知道
- Well, but my mom said it was-- - It's great, yeah, I know.

407
00:14:55,956 --> 00:14:57,657
不过你注意到她的语气了吗
But how did she say it?

408
00:14:57,657 --> 00:14:58,187
什么意思
What do you mean?

409
00:14:58,187 --> 00:15:01,927
"很好"和"还好"简直是天壤之别
There's a big difference between "It's great," and "It's great."

410
00:15:01,927 --> 00:15:02,437
你听出来了吗
You hear that?

411
00:15:02,437 --> 00:15:05,387
"很好"和"还好"
"It's great," And "It's great."

412
00:15:05,387 --> 00:15:07,397
我只知道很多人都说我很有才
All I hear is a bunch of people telling me I'm great.

413
00:15:07,427 --> 00:15:09,198
这就是问题所在了 因为很多时候
And that's a problem, because a lot of times

414
00:15:09,228 --> 00:15:11,028
人们怕你伤不起 故意说谎骗你
people will lie to you to protect your feelings,

415
00:15:11,068 --> 00:15:12,428
那对你完全没好处的
And that's not doing you any favors.

416
00:15:12,428 --> 00:15:13,938
如果想走得更远
You get a lot farther in life

417
00:15:13,938 --> 00:15:16,538
就必须明白自己的优势和劣势所在
if you know what you're good at and what you're not.

418
00:15:16,568 --> 00:15:18,488
现在能接受了吗
Now you can handle that, right?

419
00:15:19,139 --> 00:15:20,959
-恩 -就知道你可以的
- Yeah. - Of course you can.

420
00:15:21,899 --> 00:15:23,099
你还好吧 亲爱的
How you doing, honey?

421
00:15:23,099 --> 00:15:25,169
还好啦
I'm great.

422
00:15:26,369 --> 00:15:27,889
好了 大伙儿 动起来
Okay, everybody, come on!

423
00:15:28,139 --> 00:15:29,529
还有两分钟开伙 准备好哟
Two minutes till dinner! Get ready!

424
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:30,280
好啊 真棒
Good! All right!

425
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,250
哇塞 曼尼 手上端的什么啊
Oh, wow, Manny. What have you got there?

426
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,680
他亲手做的餐桌装饰哦
He made a centerpiece!

427
00:15:33,710 --> 00:15:35,850
-真了不起 -令人震惊
- Oh, that's fantastic. - It's stunning.

428
00:15:36,070 --> 00:15:37,450
就是个垃圾
It's garbage.

429
00:15:37,490 --> 00:15:38,820
别别别啊
No, no, no!

430
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,591
你干什么呀 多漂亮啊
What are you doing? It's so beautiful!

431
00:15:40,621 --> 00:15:41,891
别骗我了
Stop the lies.

432
00:15:41,891 --> 00:15:42,651
杰跟我说实话了
Jay told me the truth.

433
00:15:42,721 --> 00:15:44,061
你胡说些什么了
What did you say?

434
00:15:44,091 --> 00:15:45,561
我就说他可以做得更好啊
I mentioned it wasn't his best effort.

435
00:15:45,591 --> 00:15:46,931
他说我那是瞎胡闹
He said it was a swing and a miss.

436
00:15:46,961 --> 00:15:49,101
为什么 为什么你要泼冷水啊 杰
Why?! Why do you say these things, jay?!

437
00:15:49,101 --> 00:15:50,501
你简直跟我老妈一模一样
It's like I married my mother!

438
00:15:50,531 --> 00:15:51,952
杰 你为何那样啊
Jay, why would you do that?

439
00:15:51,952 --> 00:15:52,822
他们家人都这德行
Because he's a Pritchett.

440
00:15:52,822 --> 00:15:55,402
不过别被那些小人打击到 曼尼
But don't let these negative nellies drag you down, Manny,

441
00:15:55,572 --> 00:15:57,822
总有一天 你会想出个点石成金的创意
Because one day you could have a trillion-dollar idea

442
00:15:57,822 --> 00:16:00,562
-那些理应最爱你的人 -够了菲尔
-that the people who supposedly love you most-- - Okay, Phil!

443
00:16:01,012 --> 00:16:03,243
别说了 去拿你的头部按摩仪吧
That's it. Go get the head-scratcher.

444
00:16:03,283 --> 00:16:04,953
真正的挠头仪 "不求人"吗
The real head-scratcher, "Tm"?

445
00:16:04,983 --> 00:16:06,893
去拿过来 让大伙儿瞧瞧
Go get it, and let everybody else decide

446
00:16:06,893 --> 00:16:08,873
我耽误了你挣多少金子
how many trillions I've cost you.

447
00:16:08,873 --> 00:16:10,033
多到你想都不敢想
Way ahead of you.

448
00:16:10,323 --> 00:16:11,353
什么状况啊
What's going on here?

449
00:16:11,353 --> 00:16:14,094
我们要书写帽子的新历史了
We are about to make hat history.

450
00:16:14,124 --> 00:16:16,704
我更愿意称之为"帽史"
Or as I like to call it, "Hatstory."

451
00:16:17,384 --> 00:16:20,924
先民们无所事事 终日可以自挠头皮
Early man had hours and hours to scratch his weary head.

452
00:16:20,924 --> 00:16:24,615
而今快节奏社会 哪来时间挠
But what about today's busy times?

453
00:16:25,735 --> 00:16:27,095
谢谢你 小卢子
Thank you, squire.

454
00:16:27,095 --> 00:16:28,305
这项伟大的发明妙在何处
Great thing about this?

455
00:16:29,035 --> 00:16:30,555
你可以何时何地都戴上
You can wear it anywhere.

456
00:16:32,445 --> 00:16:33,415
开秀吧 伙计
Hit it, buddy.

457
00:16:34,055 --> 00:16:35,406
我靠
Oh!

458
00:16:35,406 --> 00:16:37,476
就像成千上万的小天使
It's like a thousand tiny angels

459
00:16:37,476 --> 00:16:38,146
在我的头皮上开舞林大会...
are line dancing on my sca--

460
00:16:40,316 --> 00:16:44,286
我去 似乎头部按摩仪出了点小故障
I... it looks like we got a slight malfunction in a rear nogginizer.

461
00:16:44,656 --> 00:16:47,217
不要啊 快关了 快关了啊伙计
Oh! Shut her down! Shut her down, buddy!

462
00:16:47,257 --> 00:16:49,637
-停不了啊 -一剪没啊 发如血啊
- It's not working! - My hair! It's got my hair!

463
00:16:49,987 --> 00:16:51,727
好吧 算了
Okay! Fine.

464
00:16:51,757 --> 00:16:53,257
我没事
That--I'm fine.

465
00:16:53,297 --> 00:16:55,908
去他妈的神奇功能吧 简直是刺破头皮的
Forgot about that feature. It's an exfoliating... scrub.

466
00:16:55,908 --> 00:16:57,718
儿子 给老爸把安全剪拿来
Buddy, can you grab the safety shears?

467
00:16:57,718 --> 00:16:59,418
我告诉你 菲尔 坚持就是胜利
You know what, Phil? Keep it up.

468
00:16:59,488 --> 00:17:01,358
同是天涯沦落人
And I admire you and Manny.

469
00:17:01,358 --> 00:17:04,268
我明白被心爱的人质疑的滋味
I know what it's like to stare down skepticism from a loved one.

470
00:17:04,268 --> 00:17:05,198
小卡 现在不是时候
Cam, not now.

471
00:17:05,228 --> 00:17:06,429
有什么不行 感恩节良辰吉日啊
Why not now? It's thanksgiving.

472
00:17:06,469 --> 00:17:08,069
家人团聚 问题爆发
Families gather. Issues come up.

473
00:17:08,229 --> 00:17:09,559
问题也是你提出来才有的啊
Only if you bring them up.

474
00:17:09,559 --> 00:17:11,679
打开天窗说亮话对谁都好
It's healthy to get things out in the open.

475
00:17:11,679 --> 00:17:13,209
你们都听过我的射南瓜轶事吧
Y'all know my punkin chunkin story,

476
00:17:13,249 --> 00:17:14,549
要不要我再帮你们复习一下
or do you need a refresher?

477
00:17:14,579 --> 00:17:15,719
-我们听过 -好几遍呢
- We've heard it. -Oh, several times.

478
00:17:15,749 --> 00:17:16,759
我喜欢那个故事
I love it.

479
00:17:16,759 --> 00:17:18,790
是和科迪还有别的朋友一起的那个吗
With Cody and the friends?

480
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:20,220
没错 所以你们知道故事结局吧
Yes. So you know how it ends.

481
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:23,390
但问题是 觉得我瞎编的举手
But the question is, who here thinks I made that up?

482
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:28,801
看吧 简直是泾渭分明 清清楚楚啊
Oh. Well, doesn't that tell the whole story right there?

483
00:17:28,801 --> 00:17:32,051
这边是我们的怀疑派 打压别人梦想的人
Here we have the skeptics, the dream-squashers...

484
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:33,341
普里契特一家
the Pritchetts.

485
00:17:33,341 --> 00:17:37,431
而这边是梦想家 艺术家和有远见的人
And here we have the dreamers, the artists, the visionaries.

486
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:38,892
苍天大地啊
Sweet Caroline!

487
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:40,642
难道要让我们相信
So we're supposed to believe that

488
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:43,942
你让一个南瓜飞过了整个足球场
you make a-a pumpkin fly across a football field.

489
00:17:43,942 --> 00:17:44,902
对 我现在就能证明给你们看
Yeah. I can prove it to you right now.

490
00:17:44,902 --> 00:17:45,742
我们去足球场
Let's go to the football field.

491
00:17:45,742 --> 00:17:47,582
行 去就去 我希望争议就此结束
Yes! Let's do this. I'd love to end this.

492
00:17:47,582 --> 00:17:48,562
就是 我们去比试一场吧
Yeah! Let's settle this!

493
00:17:48,562 --> 00:17:49,693
梦想家对普里契特一家
Dreamers versus Pritchetts!

494
00:17:49,733 --> 00:17:52,133
太棒了 我说南瓜你说射
Bravo! Bravo! When I say "Punkin," You say "Chunkin"!

495
00:17:52,163 --> 00:17:54,003
-南瓜 南瓜 -不 停下来
- Punkin! Punkin! - No, no, no!

496
00:17:54,033 --> 00:17:57,873
站住 我做了8个小时的饭菜
Hold it! I did not just cook for eight hours

497
00:17:57,873 --> 00:18:00,984
不是为了让你们跑出去证明些愚蠢的观点
so you people could run off to prove some asinine point

498
00:18:00,984 --> 00:18:03,174
输掉的那一方会很难过的
that's only gonna make half of us feel bad!

499
00:18:03,174 --> 00:18:05,774
拜托 尊重下我的劳动成果好吗
Come on! Show a little respect.

500
00:18:09,794 --> 00:18:11,425
火鸡闻起来很香 亲爱的
Turkey smells great, sweetheart.

501
00:18:11,425 --> 00:18:12,785
那是火鸡吗
Is that turkey?

502
00:18:12,795 --> 00:18:14,735
我怎么觉得闻起来像鸡味[胆小鬼]
Because something smells like chicken.

503
00:18:14,735 --> 00:18:16,595
-好吧 我们一决胜负吧 -太好了
- Okay, let's settle this. - Yeah.

504
00:18:16,595 --> 00:18:17,655
大家来吧 杰 我开车
Vamos, vamos! Jay, I drive!

505
00:18:17,665 --> 00:18:18,805
我说南瓜你说射
When I say "Punkin," You say "Chunkin"!

506
00:18:18,835 --> 00:18:19,865
南瓜 射
Punkin! Chunkin!

507
00:18:20,735 --> 00:18:22,826
简直是我经历过最酷的事儿
This is the coolest thing ever.

508
00:18:22,826 --> 00:18:24,166
我要录下来
Okay, I want to film.

509
00:18:24,426 --> 00:18:25,996
不 等一下 我也要露个脸
Ay, no, wait, I want to be in it.

510
00:18:25,996 --> 00:18:27,606
小卡 你确定这样可以吗
Hey, Cam, are you sure this is going to work?

511
00:18:27,606 --> 00:18:29,476
天呐 你说话的语气和科迪一模一样
Oh, god, you sound just like Cody.

512
00:18:30,156 --> 00:18:31,836
你觉得这个可不可以用来发射一个人
Do you think this could launch a human?

513
00:18:31,836 --> 00:18:33,107
卢克
Luke...

514
00:18:33,577 --> 00:18:35,447
-我们还是先发射南瓜吧 -好
- Let's do the pumpkin first. - Okay.

515
00:18:36,607 --> 00:18:37,417
他们在那儿玩的真开心
They're having fun over there,

516
00:18:37,447 --> 00:18:38,917
但最后肯定是悲剧结尾
but you know it's gonna end in tears.

517
00:18:38,917 --> 00:18:39,867
对 向来都是
Yeah, always does.

518
00:18:39,867 --> 00:18:41,367
敲门敲门 谁啊
Knock-knock. Who's there?

519
00:18:41,367 --> 00:18:42,127
物理学
Physics.

520
00:18:42,157 --> 00:18:43,258
-谢谢 -不用
- Thank you. - Mm-hmm.

521
00:18:43,288 --> 00:18:44,428
谁应该来发射它
Who's gonna be able to launch it?

522
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:45,558
我觉得是小卡
I think it should be Cam!

523
00:18:45,758 --> 00:18:47,038
哦不 我觉得应该是我们所有人一起
Oh, no! I think it should be all of us!

524
00:18:47,038 --> 00:18:47,898
所有人 所有人
All of us! All of us!

525
00:18:47,928 --> 00:18:49,268
到这儿来 哇
Just get right here. Whoo!

526
00:18:50,188 --> 00:18:53,338
我必须声明 我没有打压菲尔所有的梦想
For the record, I don't squash all of Phil's dreams.

527
00:18:53,338 --> 00:18:55,419
只是那些 可能会 注定悲剧的
Just the ones that are, you know, potentially fatal.

528
00:18:55,419 --> 00:18:57,319
我只是想让那孩子准备好来面对现实生活
I'm just trying to get the kid ready for life.

529
00:18:57,349 --> 00:18:59,099
对 如果我们不对他们狠一点
Yeah. Yes, I-if we didn't do this to them,

530
00:18:59,099 --> 00:19:00,529
在社会上也会撞得鼻青脸肿
the world would.

531
00:19:00,569 --> 00:19:02,539
好 大家各就各位准备好要发射了吗
Okay, everybody, in final launching positions?

532
00:19:02,569 --> 00:19:04,239
准备接受羞"乳"吧
Get ready to eat some crow!

533
00:19:04,409 --> 00:19:06,530
羞"乳"的味道可不怎么美味哦
It is not as delicious as it sounds.

534
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:08,300
好
Okay...

535
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:09,360
一
Uno!

536
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:11,510
二 三
Dos! Tres! Three!

537
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:16,711
怎么回事 小卡
What happened, Cam?

538
00:19:16,711 --> 00:19:18,471
我不知道 我 我不知道
I don't know. I-I don't know.

539
00:19:18,471 --> 00:19:19,481
我们再试一次行吗
Can we do it again?

540
00:19:19,511 --> 00:19:21,291
不 我们只有一个南瓜
No, we only had one pumpkin,

541
00:19:21,301 --> 00:19:22,531
而我们刚刚发射掉了
and we just chunk it.

542
00:19:24,281 --> 00:19:26,232
-就说嘛 我们是对的 -哈 是的
- Well, we were right. - Aw, yeah.

543
00:19:27,682 --> 00:19:28,762
对不起
I'm sorry, guys.

544
00:19:29,952 --> 00:19:31,502
通常我们赢了应该更开心才对啊 对吧
This usually feels a little better, doesn't it?

545
00:19:31,502 --> 00:19:32,892
-是的 -是吧
- Yeah. - Huh? Mm.

546
00:19:33,522 --> 00:19:34,582
好吧 虽然我不愿意承认这点
All right. I-I hate to admit it,

547
00:19:34,582 --> 00:19:36,422
但是当他们把南瓜放进去的时候
but when they put the pumpkin in,

548
00:19:36,422 --> 00:19:37,693
我有一点希望他们能成功
I was kind of hoping it would work.

549
00:19:37,693 --> 00:19:39,403
-是的 -我也是
- Yeah. - Me, too.

550
00:19:40,523 --> 00:19:42,793
好吧 开始幸灾乐祸吧
All right! Let the gloating begin.

551
00:19:42,793 --> 00:19:44,503
你知道吗 其实是一次好的尝试
You know, it was a pretty good try.

552
00:19:44,503 --> 00:19:46,073
我们不需要你们的同情
We don't need your pity.

553
00:19:46,073 --> 00:19:47,944
我们清理一下球场吧
Let's just get this stuff cleaned up.

554
00:19:47,974 --> 00:19:51,864
或者 或者我们可以
Well--or if--if maybe we, um...

555
00:19:52,754 --> 00:19:54,734
-试一下用更大的倾斜角发射 -是的
- We launch it from a steeper angle? - Yeah.

556
00:19:54,734 --> 00:19:56,374
然后 如果你们能有多一些人
Then...maybe if you had somebody else,

557
00:19:56,374 --> 00:19:57,874
一起帮你们拉它
you know, helping you pull the thing.

558
00:19:57,874 --> 00:19:59,205
但是我们没有多余的南瓜了
But we don't have any more pumpkins.

559
00:19:59,235 --> 00:20:00,535
那很简单
That's the easy part!

560
00:20:00,575 --> 00:20:03,055
街坊邻居家家户户门前都有
They're on every porch up and down the block.

561
00:20:03,055 --> 00:20:04,505
-我们可以搞定 来吧 -是的
- Oh, we can handle that. Come on, kid! - Yeah.

562
00:20:04,545 --> 00:20:05,805
来吧 让我们再试一次
Come on. Let's try one.

563
00:20:05,805 --> 00:20:07,165
好吧 我们再试一次
Okay! All right! Let's do it!

564
00:20:07,165 --> 00:20:09,526
我说南瓜大家说射
I say "Punkin," Gang says "Chunkin"!

565
00:20:09,526 --> 00:20:13,336
这个世界上有梦想家 也有现实主义者
There are dreamers and there are realists in this world.

566
00:20:13,336 --> 00:20:15,376
你可能会觉得梦想家们喜欢聚在一起
You'd think the dreamers would find the dreamers

567
00:20:15,406 --> 00:20:17,046
现实主义者又聚成另外的小集体
and the realists would find the realists,

568
00:20:17,076 --> 00:20:20,477
但是往往 二者喜欢混搭在一起
but more often than not, the opposite is true.

569
00:20:20,517 --> 00:20:21,547
如果这个成功了
Maybe if this works,

570
00:20:21,577 --> 00:20:22,887
我们下一个应该发射我做的餐桌装饰
we should launch my centerpiece next.

571
00:20:22,917 --> 00:20:24,207
它没有那么糟糕啦
It wasn't that bad.

572
00:20:24,207 --> 00:20:25,807
你做的手抓饭倒是挺糟糕的
Your rice pilaf was.

573
00:20:27,557 --> 00:20:29,427
杰 小心点儿
Jay, be careful!

574
00:20:29,457 --> 00:20:30,988
好的 准备
Okay. All right.

575
00:20:31,028 --> 00:20:34,058
好 好 继续用力 继续用力
Oh! Oh! Keep going, keep going! Keep going!

576
00:20:36,668 --> 00:20:38,228
其实 梦想家需要现实主义者
You see, the dreamers need the realists

577
00:20:38,268 --> 00:20:40,418
提醒他们 不要把梦想放飞得过高
to keep them from soaring too close to the sun.

578
00:20:40,418 --> 00:20:42,009
而现实主义者
And the realists...

579
00:20:43,039 --> 00:20:44,489
如果没有梦想家的话
Well, without the dreamers,

580
00:20:45,259 --> 00:20:47,349
可能永远无法将梦想放飞
they might not ever get off the ground.

581
00:20:50,239 --> 00:20:53,810
好 下一个一定会穿过球门
Okay! Next one's going through the--the goal thingy,

582
00:20:53,810 --> 00:20:55,450
我能感觉到
I can feel it!

583
00:20:59,110 --> 00:21:01,260
当洛娜 科迪和我做这件事的时候
Now when Lorna, Cody, and I did this, it was--

584
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:02,541
少说话 多用力
less talkin', more chunkin.

585
00:21:02,541 --> 00:21:03,491
妈妈 我要告诉你一件事
Mom, I need to tell you something.

586
00:21:03,491 --> 00:21:04,361
是什么 宝贝
What is it, honey?

587
00:21:04,361 --> 00:21:05,281
准备
Ready!

588
00:21:05,281 --> 00:21:06,851
海莉开车的时候 我让她分心了
I distracted Haley while she was driving,

589
00:21:06,851 --> 00:21:07,901
我们把你的车撞出了一个凹痕
And we dented your car.

590
00:21:07,901 --> 00:21:09,081
发射
Fire!

591
00:21:16,052 --> 00:21:17,762
姑娘们
Well, girls...

592
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:20,972
再忍三秒 就追究不到你们头上了
Three more seconds, and you would have gotten away with it.

593
00:21:22,462 --> 00:21:23,832
现在射人了吧
Now a human?

594
00:21:23,832 --> 00:21:25,193
过来吧 莉莉
Come here, Lily.

595
00:21:25,193 --> 00:21:26,533
卢克 别犯二
Luke, no.
